{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794759528,"nonce":"zpVEjihwwnNGNMIT6Vp2CSdKG38=","title":"An open overlay keeps the window drawing every frame while any CSS animation repeats anywhere in the tree","message":"`overlay_css_needs_redraw` in the windowed frame path was \"an overlay is on screen and `css_has_active()`\", and `css_has_active()` is not gated by visibility. The cn demo has eight animations that repeat with no end (progress bars, skeletons, spinners), so with a dropdown or popover open the redraw chain never parks: reported at 27% CPU with a dropdown open and the window idle.\n\n`RenderTree::css_has_active_for_overlay` counts an animation that is bound to end, one that has stopped with its final values still to be written, and one inside an overlay. An infinite animation on the page behind it is drawn while it is visible, by the signal gated on what was painted. Tests: overlay_css_active in blinc_recorder.\n\nNot measured in a window. An infinite animation inside a closed-over overlay root is the case to look at if a spinner in a popover stops animating.\n\nLabels: bug, perf, area:app.","files":null}]}